# File structure and Roc regions

**Status:** current.

A `.rocci` file may mix a module header, imports, types, helpers, and any
number of recognized declarations. Everything outside an `@` declaration is
copied into generated Roc unchanged.

```rocci
module Example exposing [hello]

import Html

Tone : [Neutral, Positive]

@component Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, {name}</p>
```

Recognized **only** at the start of a top-level definition: `@component`,
`@fixture`, `@test`, `@css`, `@context`, `@init`, and `@method:role` routes.

Roc regions (directive headers, interpolations, params, `@match` patterns)
are token ranges. The template parser does not type-check them. Parenthesize
records in directive headers so `{` is not read as the body opener.

**Errors:** unrecognized `@` at top-level stays invalid; `@` inside Markdown
is a Rocdown concern, not this file type.

**Related:** [Components](/docs/reference/language/components/),
[Tests](/docs/reference/language/tests/),
[Generated Roc](/docs/reference/language/generated-roc/).
